  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "Kbm8IKwqcKyqg019SfapFX7Xjps=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:32.291Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The scenario specifies three setup stages. Paperless first: email integration over POP/IMAP, OCR and LLM configuration, and definition of document types, tags and storage locations. Then a Powerhouse instance: Switchboard plus Connect plus a Postgres database; the `powerhouse/invoice` package providing a drive app, document editors and an analytics processor; and `powerhouse/paperless` providing a paperless integration document. Then the integration itself: set the endpoint, configure the webhook.\n\nNaming the packages matters more than it appears. A demo assembled from installable packages is reproducible by the audience, which is what separates a proof from a performance \u2014 and the packaging is the same artefact a consultancy would deploy for a client.\n\nThe scenario continues into expense invoicing (selecting invoices and receipts and turning them into invoice line items) and then automated payments.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T10:34:32.291324Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:32.291329Z"
    }
  },
